PART A. exponent conditions (strict, as g -> 0); minimal integer p_0
  (a) R on, CMP 122 II p. 383 : 2 p_1 - (d+5) r > p_0 with p_1 < p_0  <=>  p_0 > (d+5) r
  (b) R on, (1.88) merge step : p_0 > (d+2) r   [linear p_0(g_{j+1}) against R^(d+2)]
  (c) R on, (1.82) base case  : 2 p_0 > (d+2) r [quadratic p_0^2 against R^(d+2)]
  (d) R on, (1.95)            : p_0 > d r       [2 kappa (100 R_k)^d <= p_0(g_k)/4 - 1]
  (e) R = id, d = 3 (Prop. 2) : p_0 > (d+1) r   [merge], 2 p_0 > (d+1) r + 1 [base, tail <= x/ln L steps]
  (f) note 49 s5 (superseded) : 2 p_0 > (d+1) r

| d | r | (a) p_0 > (d+5)r | (b) p_0 > (d+2)r | (c) 2p_0 > (d+2)r | (d) p_0 > d r | (e) merge p_0 > (d+1)r | (e) base 2p_0 > (d+1)r+1 | (f) 2p_0 > (d+1)r |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| 3 | 2 | 17 | 11 | 6 | 7 | 9 | 5 | 5 |
| 3 | 3 | 25 | 16 | 8 | 10 | 13 | 7 | 7 |
| 4 | 2 | 19 | 13 | 7 | 9 | 11 | 6 | 6 |
| 4 | 3 | 28 | 19 | 10 | 13 | 16 | 9 | 8 |

Binding exponent, R on:   p_0 > (d+5) r :  d = 4 -> 9 r,  d = 3 -> 8 r (if R were kept at d = 3)
Binding exponent, R = id: p_0 > (d+1) r :  d = 3 -> 4 r

PART B. L-conditions of the printed geometry (CMP 122 II p. 384-385, CMP 122 I p. 193-194)
| L | 42 L/(L-1) | < 63 ? | L^(-1/2) | <= 1/2 ? | exists integer L_0 >= 2 with L_0^2 <= L/3 ? |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| 2 | 84.00 | NO | 0.7071 | NO | NO |
| 3 | 63.00 | yes | 0.5774 | NO | NO |
| 4 | 56.00 | yes | 0.5000 | yes | NO |
| 5 | 52.50 | yes | 0.4472 | yes | NO |
| 6 | 50.40 | yes | 0.4082 | yes | NO |
| 12 | 45.82 | yes | 0.2887 | yes | yes |
  (sup over n-j of 42(1-L^-(n-j))/(1-1/L) = 42L/(L-1) is never attained, so the strict '< 63' needs 42L/(L-1) <= 63, i.e. L >= 3)

PART C. 3D flow g_j^2 = g^2 L^(j-K), x_j = ln g_j^-2 = x_K + (K-j) ln L
  analytic thresholds on x_K (g^2 = exp(-x_K)):
    (B1) K-j < R_j  holds as soon as x_j >= 1 (since (x_j - x_K)/ln L < x_j/ln L <= x_j <= x_j^r)
    (B2) R_{j+1}/R_j in {1, 1/L}  needs (x/(x - ln L))^r <= L,  i.e.  x >= x_b := ln L/(1 - L^(-1/r))
    (B3) drops of R separated by >= 3 steps  needs  x >= x_c := ln L/(1 - L^(-1/(3 r)))
| L | r | x_b | x_c | g^2 = e^-x_c |
